| `runtimes.max_steps` | integer | `10000` | a whole number, 1 or more | `runtimes/_inprocess.py` (`InProcessRuntime`, `configured_max_steps`) | Sets how many steps one in-process run may take; the step past it is a `RuntimeError` naming the plan and the cap, the guard against a plan whose edges never reach its end. A `max_steps` argument to the engine overrides it. Absent, the engine writes `[using default] runtimes.max_steps = 10000` to stderr. | the `langgraph` engine, which keeps its own recursion limit; a model call's time: `models.timeout_seconds` | always |
